      "title": "Total Compensation Calculator",
      "description": "Total Compensation Calculator - SOU Human Resources SOU Home Campus Directory Map Finance & Administration Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Payroll Services Okta Login Search Human Resources HR Staff Directory HR Events Calendar Request an Appointment HR Secure Inbox Working at SOU Why SOU? Search Jobs SOU Guide to Inclusive Rogue Valley Living SOU Affiliates & Volunteers Total Compensation Calculator Perks & Discounts Verifications of Employment Employee Resources Accommodations Annual Reminders Employment and Pay Information Hiring Guide for Supervisors Holiday Schedule HR Procedures and Forms Inclement Weather & Hazardous Conditions Outstanding Staff Award Separating Employees Shared Governance Telecommuting Work Injury/Illness Learning & Development Staff Performance Management Workday HR Guides CISR Learning & Development Osher Lifelong Learning Institute University Policies Full Policy Listing Mandatory Child Abuse Reporting Office Equity Grievance & Title IX SOU Internal Auditor/EthicsPoint Emergency Response Benefits & Leaves Health Benefits Retirement Leaves Employee Assistance Program Faculty Relinquishment Menu Menu Human Resources Total Compensation Calculator Why SOU? Search Jobs Become an SOU Employee Current Student Jobs Current Faculty & Staff Jobs SOU Guide to Inclusive Rogue Valley Living SOU Affiliates & Volunteers Total Compensation Calculator Perks & Discounts Staff Tuition Public Service Loan Forgiveness Program Notary Public Services Discounts Verifications of Employment This Total Compensation Calculator below is a tool that demonstrates the significance of our benefits package and how it is an important complement to salary. [Disclaimer: This tool is intended for estimation purposes only and does not include additional perks like our Staff Tuition Program, professional development, Linkedin Learning, hardship leave, bus passes, bookstore and IT product discounts, access to Ticket Monster, campus events, and more. Part-time employment is not captured in this estimation.] Please enter your annual gross salary $ Will you be a nine-month or twelve-month employee? 9 12 Are you Classified, Administrative, or Faculty? Administrative Classified Faculty How many years have you been at SOU? 0-5 6-10 11-15 16-20 21-25 26+ Are you enrolled in a retirement program (Example: PERS) No, I have not enrolled in a retirement program Yes, PERS Tier 1 Yes, PERS Tier 2 Yes, PERS/OPSRP Retired Are you enrolled in a retirement program (Example: PERS) No, I have not enrolled in a retirement program Yes, PERS Tier 1 Yes, PERS Tier 2 Yes, PERS/OPSRP Yes, ORP Tier 1 Yes, ORP Tier 2 Yes, ORP Tier 3 Yes, ORP Tier 4 Retired Submit SOU – Paid Benefits Brief Description Estimated annual amount paid for you by SOU Comprehensive Medical, Dental, Vision, and Basic Life SOU pays 95% or 97% of premiums for you and your eligible dependents’ comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage. The Public Employee Benefits Board (PEBB) gives you a choice of plans that meet your family’s needs. You are automatically enrolled in $10,000 basic life insurance and covered through Medex, a travel insurance benefit. Retirement Holidays Vacation Leave Sick Leave You accrue 8 paid hours per month to be used for your illness or that of a qualifying family member. Employee Assistance Program Cascade Centers Inc. provides three confidential consultations per issue/concern to employees and their dependents. Includes legal and financial referrals. $12.48 Medicare, Social Security, Unemployment Insurance, Worker’s Compensation, Oregon Paid Family Medical Leave Other payroll expenses SOU funds. Total benefit dollars As a percentage of gross salary Estimated total annual compensation Contact HR Churchill Hall 159 1250 Siskiyou Boulevard Ashland, OR 97520 Email: hrs@sou.edu Phone: (541) 552-8553 Fax: (541) 552-8508 Hours: Monday-Friday, 8:00 a.m. – 5:00 p.m. [excluding university holidays] Request an Appointment Scroll to top"
